WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.957
Shell interpretation is one of the most important subprocess boundaries.

2
00:00:03.957 --> 00:00:11.243
A shell treats text as instructions with features such as parsing,
expansion, redirection, chaining, variables, and pattern matching.

3
00:00:11.243 --> 00:00:18.277
Those features are useful for interactive administration, but they are
risky when application data can influence the command text.

4
00:00:18.277 --> 00:00:25.061
The safer default is direct execution with the shell disabled, especially
when any value may come from a user or external system.

5
00:00:25.061 --> 00:00:28.452
Direct execution separates the executable from its arguments.

6
00:00:28.452 --> 00:00:35.738
The application chooses a program from trusted configuration or an
approved allowlist, then passes each argument as a structured value.

7
00:00:35.738 --> 00:00:39.569
This makes it much harder for ordinary data to become command structure.

8
00:00:39.569 --> 00:00:46.227
It also makes code review more straightforward because reviewers can see
which parts are the command and which parts are data.

9
00:00:46.227 --> 00:00:53.576
String-built command lines are fragile because they mix command syntax,
options, file paths, and untrusted values into one piece of text.

10
00:00:53.576 --> 00:01:00.108
Escaping and quoting rules vary across shells and platforms, and the
safest answer is usually to avoid needing those rules.

11
00:01:00.108 --> 00:01:11.727
When developers reach for shell conveniences such as pipelines, globbing,
variable expansion, or redirection, they should ask whether Python APIs or
explicit process handling can provide the same result more safely.

12
00:01:11.727 --> 00:01:19.076
There are cases where shell features are genuinely required, but they
should be treated as exceptions that need justification and review.

13
00:01:19.076 --> 00:01:27.995
The operation should be narrow, inputs should be mapped to approved
choices, secrets should not be placed into command text, and the runtime
should use least privilege.

14
00:01:27.995 --> 00:01:35.720
Avoiding shell interpretation does not solve every subprocess risk, but it
removes a large class of unintended parsing behavior from the design.
